Subject: [PATCH] phy: rockchip: skip state sampling without a linestate register

The RK3128 host port has no utmi_ls register in the PHY configuration.
Do not read GRF offset zero and mistake its value for a USB line state.
Keep the port active, matching the guard in the working KNULLI driver
(local reference 72498e26, phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c).

--- a/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/rockchip/phy-rockchip-inno-usb2.c
@@ -932,6 +932,9 @@
 	unsigned int ul_mask, uhd_mask;
 	int ret;
 
+	if (!rport->port_cfg->utmi_ls.offset)
+		return;
+
 	mutex_lock(&rport->mutex);
 
 	ret = regmap_read(rphy->grf, rport->port_cfg->utmi_ls.offset, &ul);
